      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To clarify, the last update disabled the video player (I think), its true that the video player used to cause instability on linux systems so the workaround was to rename/remove youtube-dl. Now that proton has partial windows-mf support the video players don't cause crashing. Soonish proton will have full wmf support (including evr) and I worry that vrchat videos still wont play cause the video player has been manually disabled when running in proton.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
